You can use your own distance measure by creating a variable in the dataset with that distance measure (e.g. a propensity score estimated in some other way) and then sending that to matchit using the distance option, like this:

http://r.iq.harvard.edu/docs/matchit/2.4-20/How_Do_I3.html

It will look something like

m.out <- matchit(treat ~ x1 + x2, data=dataset, distance=dataset$myownmeasure)

The treat ~ x1 + x2 formula is then used just to tell matchit what the treatment variable is and what the covariates to check balance on are.

Thanks,
Liz


